<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto p-6 space-y-3">
  <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold">Skill Capture for Microsoft Office</h1>
  <p>Skill Capture adds a <strong>Skills</strong> button to the Home tab in Excel, Word and PowerPoint. From the pane you can browse your team's skill library, record a procedure for others to reuse, and (as a reviewer) approve captured workflows.</p>
  <h2 class="font-semibold">What is collected</h2>
  <p>Only when you turn on <em>Capture my workflow</em> or record a procedure: the <em>type</em> of each step (for example "Sort data" or "Add a slide") and when it happened. Never file names, sheet names, cell values or document text. Changes made by co-authors are ignored. Steps you type while recording are sent as you wrote them.</p>
  <h2 class="font-semibold">Need help?</h2>
  <p>Contact your Skill Capture administrator.</p>
</div>
